{"kind": "prediction", "attempt_id": "agent-20261118T060622Z-02", "source": "agent", "trial_id": "agent-20261118T060622Z", "attempt": 2, "file": "packages/core/core-flows/src/cart/utils/prepare-confirm-inventory-input.ts", "cause": "per-line-check", "hypothesis": "formatInventoryInput checks availability per cart line (MathBN.gte of stock against required_quantity times item.quantity) and never adds up lines that share an inventory item. OVS-PIECE (1 WIDGET) and OVS-TWOPACK (2 WIDGET) both draw on the shared WIDGET item, with 10 stocked. Two carts, one ordering 6 PIECE plus 0 and another ordering 6 TWOPACK (12 units), each pass the per-line check alone against 10 units, so if both complete the run promises 18 WIDGET units from 10. I expect no_oversell to fail when both carts complete, since the sum of their needs exceeds the stock. Simpler: one cart with 6 PIECE and 3 TWOPACK (12 units) on a single line set should also pass the per-line check. I test two carts so the race is between them.", "scenario_sha256": "6a3320e7dfeb7bc6cbfa7b4c1ff9245170cbb1ce3c861619fb12648ae725c629", "expected_check": "no_oversell", "refused": null, "timestamp": "2026-11-18T06:09:41+00:00"}
